# Pre-commit / pre-push: run tests first

Before any `git commit` or `git push` requested by the user:

1. Run the relevant automated tests for the changed code (prefer unit/logic tests under `app/src/test`; run UI/e2e when those surfaces changed).
2. Default command when unsure: `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` (or the project’s equivalent).
3. **Do not commit** if tests fail. Fix failures first, then re-run until green.
4. Mention in the reply which test command ran and that it passed (or why a layer was skipped in one line).

Never skip this step because the change “looks small.”
